# Supabase connection (optional for local dev).
# When these are set, the app persists to your Supabase Postgres and uses
# Supabase Auth for accounts. When left empty, the app falls back to local
# accounts and data in this browser (localStorage).
#
# Find both in Supabase: Project Settings > API (or > API Keys).
#   VITE_SUPABASE_URL      = Project URL, e.g. https://abcdefgh.supabase.co
#   VITE_SUPABASE_ANON_KEY = the "anon public" key (or "publishable" key, sb_publishable_...)
#
# NEVER put the service_role / secret key (sb_secret_...) here. Everything
# prefixed VITE_ is bundled into the website and readable by anyone.
# The app refuses to start Supabase with a secret key.
#
# After filling these in: run supabase/schema.sql, then `npm run check:supabase`.
VITE_SUPABASE_URL=
VITE_SUPABASE_ANON_KEY=
